Spetum is the best polearm for damage-to-weight ratio.  Since it's
generated in the initial inventory of 1 in 8 trolls it's not uncommon
for my characters to have one by the time they do the two castles.  For
killing water monsters your level of skill hardly matters.  Stand there
and hit them until they die.  With Croesus that would involve trading
blows so I prefer using a wand on him.  I've used a spetum at the draw
bridge but eventually a monster gets past and it turns into a melee
battle.  After that experience I'd rather thin the advancing crowd with
missiles, wands and spells.

Where the lance beats any polearm is at expert level.  At expert it
works apllying it at range 1.  So the hard part is exercising it up to
that point.  I've played knights that didn't bother.


